{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And HaShem spoke to Aaron: And I, behold, I have given you the charge of My gift-offerings.</b> Here He confirmed the priesthood for him after challengers had risen against it. A parable: to what may the matter be compared? To a king who gave a field to his friend but did not write or sign the deed for him, and someone came and challenged him. The king said to him: whoever wishes to challenge may challenge — behold, I am writing and signing for him. So here, He gave him the twenty-four gifts of the priesthood. Thus the Rabbis of blessed memory expounded in the chapter HaZeru'a: twenty-four gifts of the priesthood there are, and all of them were given to Aaron and to his sons by general statement and particular statement and the covenant of salt. Whoever fulfills them is as if he fulfilled the general and the particular and the covenant of salt, and whoever transgresses them is as if he transgressed the general and the particular and the covenant of salt. And these are they: ten gifts in the Temple, and ten in the provinces, and four in Jerusalem. Ten in the Temple: the sin-offering of an animal, the sin-offering of a bird, a definite guilt-offering, a suspended guilt-offering, the peace-offerings of the congregation, the log of oil of the leper, the two loaves, the showbread, the remainder of meal-offerings, the remainder of the omer. Four in Jerusalem: the firstborn, the first fruits, the ram of the nazirite, the hides of the consecrated animals. Ten in the provinces: תרומה (the heave-offering), תרומת מעשר (the heave-offering of the tithe), חלה (the dough-offering), ראשית הגז (the first of the fleece), and the gifts that are the foreleg and the cheeks and the stomach, the redemption of the son, the firstborn of a donkey, an inherited field, a field of devoted things, robbery of the convert."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:33:49.325226669Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}